From dc9be6b7a9bdae45d29d1f8dea7fba5e093e8abb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:47:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rd: frame generation moves characters with their bones

- each step mark also carries every character's bones (the character table, each model's bone list: the parent's place and the
  world matrix; PS2_FRAME_GEN_BONES=TABLE,COUNT,MODEL, Raw Danger's by default)
- per refresh: a sphere per character and, per bone, its segment and the matrix from the step drawn to the moment shown (the
  bone's matrix blended between the two steps); a pixel within 35 cm of a bone moves with it, turn included (interp.wgsl binding 4)
- gaps filled from 6 game pixels past the first landed one (the motion blur's trail and blended edges)
- Settings > Debug: a fourth view, the pixels moved with a bone in a colour each; the log counts the bones

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
